An .http file (sometimes called an HTTP Request file) is a plain-text file used by developers to write, document, and execute HTTP requests directly within their code editor. [1] (https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/explanation-http-file-net-9-sai-reddy-lqo0c), [2] (https://www.rahulpnath.com/blog/http-files-asp-net-core-dotnet)Instead of opening external applications like Postman or Insomnia, you can use these lightweight files to test your web APIs and check responses immediately without leaving your development environment. 
